GCC 15 makes the mismatch between a K&R empty-param declaration/definition and
a function-pointer type that carries explicit parameters a hard error
(previously an implicit-function-declaration warning that could be suppressed).

ngx_http_vod_module.c line ~219 declares:
    static void ngx_http_vod_exit_process();
and the definition at line ~3328 also uses empty parens.  Both are assigned to
struct slots typed `void (*)(ngx_cycle_t *)` (init/exit_process, exit_master),
so GCC 15 / core26 rejects the compilation unit outright.

Fix: give declaration and definition the explicit `(ngx_cycle_t *cycle)` signature
matching the struct's function-pointer type; silence the unused-param diagnostic
with the conventional nginx `(void) cycle;` guard.

Trip-wire: if upstream nginx-vod-module ever fixes this prototype the patch will
fail to apply (context mismatch), surfacing the redundancy immediately at build
time -- intentional per M4 review guidance.

Applies to: nginx-vod-module 1.31
GCC version that exposed this: gcc-15 (Ubuntu 25.04 / core26)
Author: Frigate snap M4 portability fix (not upstream vod patch)

--- a/ngx_http_vod_module.c
+++ b/ngx_http_vod_module.c
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@
 static ngx_int_t ngx_http_vod_run_state_machine(ngx_http_vod_ctx_t *ctx);
 static ngx_int_t ngx_http_vod_send_notification(ngx_http_vod_ctx_t *ctx);
 static ngx_int_t ngx_http_vod_init_process(ngx_cycle_t *cycle);
-static void ngx_http_vod_exit_process();
+static void ngx_http_vod_exit_process(ngx_cycle_t *cycle);
 
 static ngx_int_t ngx_http_vod_init_file_reader_with_fallback(ngx_http_request_t *r, ngx_str_t* path, uint32_t flags, void** context);
 static ngx_int_t ngx_http_vod_init_file_reader(ngx_http_request_t *r, ngx_str_t* path, uint32_t flags, void** context);
@@ -3324,9 +3324,10 @@
 	return NGX_OK;
 }
 
-static void 
-ngx_http_vod_exit_process()
+static void
+ngx_http_vod_exit_process(ngx_cycle_t *cycle)
 {
+	(void) cycle;
 #if (VOD_HAVE_ICONV)
 	webvtt_exit_process();
 #endif // VOD_HAVE_ICONV
